cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CXRQuant, please cite the IJIES article and this software release."
title: "CXRQuant: Finding-Level Stability Auditing of Reduced-Precision Inference for Radiology Impression Generation"
version: "2.3.0"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/juntazen/CXRQuant"
abstract: >-
  CXRQuant re-executes one trained source checkpoint under FP32, FP16, BitsAndBytes INT8 and NF4 and reports lexical
  similarity, FP32-relative finding stability (false-negative and false-positive flip rates), reference agreement and
  efficiency separately. Release 2.3.0 accompanies the second-round revision of the IJIES article: five training
  seeds, decoding-corrected and impression-only-loss reruns, hierarchical statistics, a randomised efficiency
  re-measurement, a LoRA-fine-tuned 7B model and CheXagent-8b on IU-XRAY and NIH ChestX-ray14, with deterministic CPU
  verification of every reported number. FP32 agreement is not clinical correctness.
keywords:
  - Model quantization
  - Clinical natural language processing
  - Reproducible benchmarking
  - chest X-ray
  - radiology report generation
  - quantization
  - reduced-precision inference
  - finding-level evaluation
  - reproducibility
